            "review_title": "Review at Nam An Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Charlesquil\nDublin, California305 contributions\n0\nAn excellent Vietnamese restaurant at Ben Thanh Market\nJul 2017 • Business\nOn a business lunch, we supposed to sit at RuNam Bistro on the 1st floor but accidentally ended up at Nam An Restaurant on the 4th floor of the same building!\nNam An serve real Vietnamese cuisine in a very nice and elegant decorated atmosphere! We love the smoking prawns in clay pot as well as fish cake La Vong style. Surprising enough, there were not too many customers dủing my lunch time there. Later, one of the staff introduced us to a hair salon on the 6th floor, and then we discovered ourselves a concept store on the 7th! Will review these later once I visit them.\nBack to Nam An Restaurant, I think this can be a 5 star rated restaurant if they do better marketing. They have good food, beautifully set up, charming service, and good location (opposite to the famous Ben Thanh Market).\nRead more\nWritten August 17, 2017",
